WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.069
STEWART BRAND: One of the thick points you made about the Fertile Crescent, where the original,

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:10.469
in a sense, the first cities took shape, is that it was later referred to as the 'Fragile

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:15.809
Crescent' because of, basically, climate
instability in that area. And how does a

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:18.740
Fragile Crescent play out in terms of cities?

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.300
MONICA SMITH: So the idea of, you know, we all

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.380
grew up with Mesopotamia as the
Fertile Crescent, "hilly flanks of the

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.859
Fertile Crescent," which made it sound like it was this ideal place for

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:31.830
cities to come up. And then all the archaeologists who went to work there

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.059
and said, "Oh god, it's really hot, it's drought, the farmers keep

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:40.829
losing their crops and it burns," and so
on. "This is not fertile, this is awful!"

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:46.230
So it's an archaeologist, Tony Wilkinson
and his group, who came up with the idea

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:51.149
of the Fragile Crescent. Oh! Now that's really interesting. Because it

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:57.149
suggests that cities come up not in
places that are really wonderful, but in

00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:02.129
places that have some kind of problem, right? So immediately you think

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:05.880
of something like New Orleans, right? New Orleans probably really ought not to

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.830
still exist. But people just keep going
back and mopping it up, because it has

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:20.600
something that overcomes that liability.
So maybe cities thrive and survive

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:27.299
because they are inherently dependent on creativity to exist at all. I think

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.890
that's a really wild idea: that synergy of creativity is what

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.570
makes cities persist. If you think about
in the last thousand years, there is not

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.020
a single city that has been abandoned,
except for maybe Chernobyl.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.530
 

